'''''Euphorbia falcata''''' ('''sickle spurge'''), is a species of ''[[Euphorbia]]'', native to most of [[Europe]], northern [[Africa]], and [[Asia]], and naturalised in other parts of the world.<ref>{{cite book |last1=United States Department of Agriculture |title=Weed Risk Assessment for Euphorbia falcata L. (Euphorbiaceae) – Sickle spurge |date=2016 |publisher=United States Department of Agriculture Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service |location=Raleigh |pages=23 pp |url=https://www.aphis.usda.gov/sites/default/files/euphorbia-falcata.pdf |access-date=10 February 2023}}</ref>

Two subspecies are recognised:<ref name ="powo">{{cite web |title=Euphorbia falcata L. |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:332094-2 |website=Plants of the World Online (POWO) |access-date=10 February 2023}}</ref>
* ''Euphorbia falcata'' subsp. ''falcata'': throughout the range of the species
* ''Euphorbia falcata'' subsp. ''macrostegia'' (Bornm.) O.Schwartz: restricted to [[Cyprus]] and western [[Turkey]]

